20. DOMINANT VULNERABILITY

This is the key innovation.

Instead of simply saying:

“You should save more.”

The system should identify the biggest vulnerability.

Possible outputs:

Liquidity Vulnerability

«“Your family may have healthcare protection, but the amount of immediately accessible savings may be insufficient for a moderate medical expense.”»

Recommended action:

«“Build a dedicated health reserve gradually.”»

OR:

Coverage Uncertainty

«“Your family has healthcare protection, but the exact coverage available for specific expenses is unclear.”»

Recommended action:

«“Review your policy/scheme coverage and verify applicable benefits.”»

OR:

Recurring Healthcare Burden

«“Recurring healthcare expenses are consuming a meaningful portion of your household healthcare budget.”»

Recommended action:

«“Track recurring expenses and review available benefits and coverage.”»

OR:

Debt Pressure

«“Existing financial obligations may reduce your ability to absorb a sudden healthcare expense.”»

Recommended action:

«“Build liquidity gradually and avoid relying solely on high-cost borrowing.”»

